n between? None — adjacent diagonally. So no pieces to flip unless a longer line exists. Actually, placing at B4 allows: vertically? No. Horizontally? B3=., B5=*, B6=@ — so B4 to B5=* and B6=@ → placing @ at B4 would sandwich B5 between B4 and B6. Yes! So B4 flips B5 (*), with B6 (@) on the right. Valid and flips one piece. Also connects to C4 and C5 below. Solid.\n- (B,7): Currently B7=., surrounded by B6=@, C7=*. Placing @ at B7 would look down: C7=*, D7=*, E7=., F7=., G7=. — no @ beyond. Left: B6=@ — adjacent, no flip. Up: A7=. — dead end. Diagonals: A6=. — no. C6=* — not helpful. C8=* — no. So does B7 connect anywhere? Down-right: C8=* — no. Up-left: A6=. — no. Wait — vertical: above B7 is A7=., below is C7=*. But D7=*, E7=?, F7=?, G7=? — E7 is empty, F7 is empty. No @ beyond the *s. So how is B7 valid? Unless... horizontal: B6=@, B7=new @, B8=* — so B8 is *, but no further @ — can't sandwich. Unless it's already listed as valid, so perhaps there's a path. Wait — diagonal: from B7 to C6? C6=*, D5=@ — yes! B7-C6-D5: B7=@, C6=*, D5=@ — so diagonal southwest: B7 to D5 via C6. C6 is *, D5 is @ — so placing @ at B7 sandwiches C6 between B7 and D5. Yes! So B7 flips C6 (*). One piece flipped. Also strengthens upper right.\n- (C,7): Currently ., below D7=*, E7=?, F7=?, G7=? — D7=*, E7=., F7=., G7=. — no @ beyond. Left: C6=*, C5=@ — so C7 to C6 to C5: C7=@, C6=*, C5=@ → sandwiches C6. Yes — flips one piece. Also connects vertically to D7=*, but no further. Horizontal: B7=., D7=* — so only left to C5 works. Still valid, flips one.\n- (E,7): Similar to C7. E7=., left: E6=*, E5=@ — so placing @ at E7 would sandwich E6 between E7 and E5. Yes — flips E6. Also, diagonal? D6=@ — so D6=@, E7=new @ — adjacent, no flip. But vertical line suffices. Flips one.\n- (F,7): F7=., left: F6=@, so placing @ at F7 with F6=@ adjacent — but to flip, need opponent beyond. F8=. — nothing. Up: E7=?, D7=* — D7=*, C7=., B7=., A7=. — no @ beyond. Diagonal: E6=* — F7-E6-D5: E6=*, D5=@ — so yes, F7=@